    {
      "keyPath": "gradeHistory.noAttempts",
      "source": "No previous attempts",
      "translations": {
        "claude": "過去の受験記録はありません",
        "gpt": "以前の試行はありません",
        "gemma": "tags.\n\n    Result: これまでの試行はありません\n\n    Actually, \"これまでの試行はありません\" is slightly wordy for a UI element.\n    \"試行履歴はありません\" (There is no attempt history) is very common in Japanese UI for \"No [X] history\".\n    However, the source is \"No previous attempts\", not \"No attempt history\".\n    \"これまでの試行はありません\" is the most faithful translation.\n\n    Let's look at \"No previous attempts\" again.\n    If I am a user looking at my grade history, and I see \"No previous attempts\", I expect to see \"これまでの試行はありません\".\n\n    One more thought: \"受験履歴はありません\" is very common if it's a test. \"回答履歴はありません\" if it's a quiz. \"試行\" is the most neutral.\n\n    Let's go with \"これまでの試行はありません\".\n\n    Wait, I should check if \"試行\" sounds too \"technical/experimental\".\n    In many Japanese LMS, \"attempt\" is translated as \"受験\" (for exams) or \"回答\" (for quizzes).\n    But \"試行\" is the standard translation for \"attempt\" in the context of \"number of attempts\".\n    Example: \"Attempt 1\" -> \"試行 1\".\n\n    Let's refine:\n    \"これまでの試行はありません\"\n\n    Actually, \"これまでの試行はありません\" is perfect.\n\n    One alternative: \"これまでの履歴はありません\" (There is no previous history). But that loses the \"attempts\" part.\n\n    Let's stick to \"これまでの試行はありません\".\n\n    Wait, I'll check if \"試行\" is used in Japanese eLearning.\n    Moodle (a major LMS) uses \"試行\" or \"受験\".\n    If the key is `gradeHistory.noAttempts`, it's definitely about the attempts.\n\n    Final decision: これまでの試行はありません.\n\n    Wait, looking at the source \"No previous attempts\", it's a fragment.\n    In Japanese, fragments are often used, but the instruction says \"Use です/ます form for polite-formal tone\".\n    \"これまでの試行はありません\" uses \"ありません\" (polite).\n\n    Final check:\n    Source: No previous attempts\n    Target: これまでの試行はありません\n    Tone: Polite-formal (Yes)\n    Placeholders: None (Yes)\n    Only Japanese: Yes.\n\n    One more check: Is \"試行\" the best word for \"attempts\" in a workbook?\n    A workbook usually involves \"answering\" (回答).\n    However, \"attempts\" is a very specific term in LMS (Attempt 1, Attempt 2).\n    In that specific context, \"試行\" is the correct technical term.\n\n    Let's consider \"これまでの回答はありません\" (No previous answers).\n    \"これまでの試行はありません\" (No previous attempts).\n    \"試行\" is safer as a translation for \"attempts\".\n\n    Final string: これまでの試行はありません\n\n    Wait, I just realized \"No previous attempts\" could also be \"これまでの試行はありません\" or \"過去の試行はありません\". \"これまでの\" is more natural for \"previous\" in a \"so far\" sense.\n\n    Let's verify \"polite-formal\".\n    \"ありません\" is the polite form of \"ない\".\n    \"です/ます\" form is requested.\n    \"ありません\" is the \"masu\" form of the verb \"ある\" (negated).\n\n    Final check on \"No previous attempts\" -> \"これまでの試行はありません\".\n\n    One more possibility: \"試行履歴はありません\" (There is no attempt history).\n    Given the key `gradeHistory.noAttempts`, \"試行履歴はありません\" is extremely natural for a UI.\n    But \"これまでの試行はありません\" is a more direct translation of the source text.\n    Usually, in localization, we prioritize the source text's meaning unless it's clearly a label.\n    \"No previous attempts\" is a status message.\n    \"これまでの試行はありません\" is a perfect status message.\n\n    Let's try to see if \"試行\" is too \"scientific\".\n    In many contexts, \"attempt\" is \"挑戦\" (challenge). But \"挑戦はありません\" sounds like \"You haven't challenged anything\", which is weird.\n    \"受験\" is for exams.\n    \"回答\" is for answers.\n    \"試行\" is the standard for \"attempts\" in software.\n\n    I will provide \"これまでの試行はありません\".\n\n    Wait, I'll check one more thing. Is \"No previous attempts\" a heading or a message?\n    If it's a message in a list, \"これまでの試行はありません\" is perfect.\n\n    Final check of the prompt:\n    \"Return ONLY the Japanese translation, nothing else\"\n    \"Preserve ALL placeholders\"\n    \"Match the specified tone: polite-formal\"\n    \"Use です/ます form\"\n    \"DO NOT add quotes, explanations, or extra formatting\"\n\n    Okay.\n\n    One last thought: \"これまでの試行はありません\" vs \"これまでの試行はございません\".\n    \"ございません\" is even more formal (Keigo).\n    \"です/ます\" is requested. \"ありません\" is the standard \"masu\" form.\n\n    Final string: これまでの試行はありません.<T>これまでの試行はありません",
        "consensus": "過去の受験記録はありません"
      },
